duckport runs SQL against a DuckDB database file. It reads requests on
standard input and writes JSON on standard output, so that an Erlang or
Elixir application can run it as a port.

In its line mode each input line is one SQL statement. With --jsonl it
speaks a versioned request protocol: correlated requests, parameterised
queries, and batches of statements committed in one transaction, each
acknowledged only once it is durable. jsonl_port is the Elixir client
for that protocol.

DuckDB 2.0 is built in from source.
